  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/freeze conditions are probable Monday night \nand Tuesday night \n\nThe coldest air of the early Autumn season is poised to arrive \nby early next week with frost/freeze conditions expected Monday \nnight and Tuesday night over much of the forecast area. \nLocations to the northwest of I-81 have the highest odds for \nfrost with min temps around the freezing mark in the northern \ntier.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n \nKEY MESSAGE 2: Little to no rainfall forecast through Oct. 9th\n\nIncreasingly moist low level southeast flow will bring low\nclouds and some light rain to areas along and east of the\nAllegheny Front later tonight through Sunday. Total QPF is \n<0.10 inch. This is the only precip fcst for the next 7 days.\n\nSecondary cold front followed by colder WNW flow could bring a\ncouple of showers downwind of Lake Erie Sunday night into early\nMonday. Otherwise, we continue to have high confidence in a \nprolonged dry stretch through next week as a large area of \nCanadian high pressure dominates the pattern.",
